.TH 0AD 6 "2026-10-05" "0\~A.D." "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
0ad \- A real-time strategy game of ancient warfare
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 0ad
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATHS " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
0\~A.D. is a free, open-source, cross-platform real-time strategy game
of ancient warfare. As the military leader of an ancient civilisation,
you must gather the resources you need to raise a military force
capable of dominating your enemies.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Basic gameplay
.TP
.B \-autostart=...
Load a map instead of showing main menu (see below).
.TP
.B \-editor
Launch the Atlas scenario editor.
.TP
.B \-mod=NAME
Start the game using NAME mod.
.TP
.B \-quickstart
Load faster (disables audio and some system info logging).
.SS Autostart
.TP
.B \-autostart=\(dqTYPEDIR/MAPNAME\(dq
Enable autostart and set MAPNAME; TYPEDIR is skirmishes, scenarios, or random.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-seed=SEED
Set randomization seed value (default 0, use \-1 for random).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-ai=PLAYER:AI
Set the AI for PLAYER (e.g. 2:petra).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-aidiff=PLAYER:DIFF
Set the difficulty of PLAYER's AI (default 3, 0: sandbox, 5: very hard).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-aiseed=AISEED
Set the seed used for the AI random generator (default 0, use \-1 for random).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-player=NUMBER
Set the playerID in non-networked games (default 1, use \-1 for observer).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-civ=PLAYER:CIV
Set PLAYER's civilisation to CIV (skirmish and random maps only).
Use random for a random civ.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-team=PLAYER:TEAM
Set the team for PLAYER (e.g. 2:2).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-ceasefire=NUM
Set a ceasefire duration NUM (default 0 minutes).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-nonvisual
Disable any graphics and sounds.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-visibility=TYPE
Set the map visibility (explored, hidden, revealed, allied, allied\-explored).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-speed=SPEED
Set the sim rate speed (default 1, max 2 in normal mode, 20 in observer mode).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-victory=SCRIPTNAME
Set the victory conditions with SCRIPTNAME located in
simulation/data/settings/victory_conditions/ (default conquest).
When the only given SCRIPTNAME is "endless", no victory conditions will apply.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-wonderduration=NUM
Set the victory duration NUM for wonder victory condition (default 10 minutes).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-relicduration=NUM
Set the victory duration NUM for relic victory condition (default 10 minutes).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-reliccount=NUM
Set the number of relics for relic victory condition (default 2 relics).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-revealed=BOOL
Set whether the map should be revealed.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-disable\-replay
Disable saving of replays.
.SS Multiplayer
.TP
.B \-autostart\-playername=NAME
Set local player NAME (default 'anonymous').
.TP
.B \-autostart\-host
Set multiplayer host mode.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-host\-players=NUMBER
Set NUMBER of human players for multiplayer game (default 2).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-client=IP
Set multiplayer client to join host at given IP address.
.SS Random maps only
.TP
.B \-autostart\-size=TILES
Set random map size in TILES (default 192).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-players=NUMBER
Set NUMBER of players on random map (default 2).
.TP
.B \-autostart\-placement=PLACEMENT
Set the placement type for a random map.
.TP
.B \-autostart\-biome=BIOME
Set the biome for a random map.
.SS RL client
.TP
.B \-rl\-interface
Run the RL interface (see source/tools/rlclient).
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B \-conf=KEY:VALUE
Set a config value.
.TP
.B \-nosound
Disable audio.
.TP
.B \-shadows
Enable shadows.
.TP
.B \-vsync
Enable VSync, i.e. lock FPS to monitor refresh rate.
.TP
.B \-xres=N
Set screen X resolution to 'N'.
.TP
.B \-yres=N
Set screen Y resolution to 'N'.
.SS Installing mods
.TP
.B PATHS
Install mods located at PATHS.
For instance:
.B 0ad mod1.pyromod mod2.zip
.SS Advanced / diagnostic
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version of the engine and exit.
.TP
.B \-dumpSchema
Create a file entity.rng in the working directory, containing
complete entity XML schema, used by various analysis tools.
.TP
.B \-entgraph
(disabled)
.TP
.B \-listfiles
(disabled)
.TP
.B \-profile=NAME
(disabled)
.TP
.B \-replay=PATH
Non-visual replay of a previous game, used for analysis purposes.
PATH is system path to commands.txt containing simulation log.
.TP
.B \-replay\-visual=PATH
Visual replay of a previous game, used for analysis purposes.
PATH is system path to commands.txt containing simulation log.
.TP
.B \-writableRoot
Store runtime game data in root data directory (only use if you
have write permissions on that directory).
.TP
.B \-ooslog
Dump simulation state in binary and ASCII representations each turn,
files created in sim_log within the game's log folder.
NOTE: game will run much slower with this option!
.TP
.B \-serializationtest=N
Check simulation state for serialization errors starting at turn N;
on test failure, error is displayed and logs created in oos_log within
the game's log folder.
NOTE: game will run much slower with this option!
.TP
.B \-rejointest=N
Simulate a rejoin and check simulation state each turn for serialization
errors; this is similar to a serialization test but much faster and
less complete. It should be enough for debugging most rejoin OOSes.
.TP
.B \-unique\-logs
Add unix timestamp and process id to the filename of mainlog.html,
interestinglog.html and oos_dump.txt to prevent these files from
becoming overwritten by another pyrogenesis process.
.TP
.B \-hashtest\-full=X
Whether to enable computation of full hashes in replaymode (default true).
Can be disabled to improve performance.
.TP
.B \-hashtest\-quick=X
Whether to enable computation of quick hashes in replaymode (default false).
Can be enabled for debugging purposes.
.TP
.B \-fixed\-frame\-frequency=F
Fix the frame time. With this flag it equals to 1/F.
For example, if F=60 it means the game behaves like it's always
running with 60 FPS.
.SS Archive builder
.TP
.B \-archivebuild=PATH
System PATH of the base directory containing mod data to be
archived/precached.
Specify all mods it depends on with
.BR \-mod= NAME .
.TP
.B \-archivebuild\-output=PATH
System PATH to output of the resulting .zip archive (use with
.BR \-archivebuild ).
.TP
.B \-archivebuild\-compress
Enable deflate compression in the .zip (no zip compression by
default since it hurts compression of release packages).
.SH EXAMPLES
1) "Bob" will host a 2 player game on the Arcadia map:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0ad \-autostart="scenarios/arcadia" \-autostart\-host \e
    \-autostart\-host\-players=2 \-autostart\-playername="Bob"
.fi
.RE
.PP
"Alice" joins the match as player 2:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0ad \-autostart\-client=127.0.0.1 \-autostart\-playername="Alice"
.fi
.RE
.PP
The players use the developer overlay to control players.
.PP
2) Load Alpine Lakes random map with random seed, 2 players (Athens and
Britons), and player 2 is PetraBot:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0ad \-autostart="random/alpine_lakes" \-autostart\-seed=\-1 \e
    \-autostart\-players=2 \-autostart\-civ=1:athen \-autostart\-civ=2:brit \e
    \-autostart\-ai=2:petra
.fi
.RE
.PP
3) Observe the PetraBot on a triggerscript map:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0ad \-autostart="random/jebel_barkal" \-autostart\-seed=\-1 \e
    \-autostart\-players=2 \-autostart\-civ=1:athen \-autostart\-civ=2:brit \e
    \-autostart\-ai=1:petra \-autostart\-ai=2:petra \-autostart\-player=\-1
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/0ad/config/local.cfg
User specific settings. You may put in this file any user specific
settings using the same syntax of the default settings file.
.PP
0\~A.D. also uses the
.BR ~/.cache/0ad/ ,
.B ~/.config/0ad/
and
.B \%~/.local/share/0ad/
directories for other user specific files, such as texture cache,
screenshots and saved games.
